# Coding Standards

## Domain Models

- Use immutable dataclasses (`frozen=True`)
- Use `slots=True`
- Prefer properties over mutable fields
- Keep models free of business logic

---

## Engines

Each engine must:

- Have one responsibility
- Be deterministic
- Avoid side effects
- Return immutable results

---

## Configuration

- No magic numbers
- All thresholds belong in configuration objects

---

## Testing

- Test-first whenever possible
- Every helper should have unit tests
- Cover edge cases
- Prefer many small tests over few large tests

---

## Evidence Objects

Every intelligence engine should expose evidence describing how conclusions were reached.

Examples:

- SwingEvidence
- StructuralLevelEvidence
- Future LiquidityEvidence

---

## Style

- No print() inside engines
- Clear function names
- Small methods
- Type hints everywhere
- Prefer composition over inheritance